    <div class="container">

        <h1>HRMS Attendance System</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">Complete Technical Feature Documentation</p>

        <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
        <ol>
            <li><a href="#overview">System Overview</a></li>
            <li><a href="#attendance">Attendance Management</a></li>
            <li><a href="#biometric">Biometric Integration</a></li>
            <li><a href="#manual-punch">Manual Punch Control</a></li>
            <li><a href="#shifts">Shifts & Duty Rosters</a></li>
            <li><a href="#policy">Attendance Policies</a></li>
            <li><a href="#leave">Leave Management</a></li>
            <li><a href="#holidays">Public Holiday Management</a></li>
            <li><a href="#payroll-integration">Payroll Integration</a></li>
            <li><a href="#sync">Data Synchronisation</a></li>
            <li><a href="#reports">Reports & Analytics</a></li>
            <li><a href="#admin">Administrative Tools</a></li>
            <li><a href="#api">API Reference</a></li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="overview">1. System Overview</h2>

        <h3>Core Architecture</h3>
        <p>
            The Attendance System is built on Laravel framework and serves as a specialised module for managing employee
            attendance, leaves, shifts, and rosters. It integrates with an external Payroll system to maintain employee
            data consistency and facilitate salary calculations.
        </p>

        <h4>Technology Stack</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Framework:</strong> Laravel (PHP)</li>
            <li><strong>Database:</strong> MySQL/MariaDB</li>
            <li><strong>Queue System:</strong> Laravel Queue (for async processing)</li>
            <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Laravel Sanctum (API), SSO Support</li>
            <li><strong>Excel Processing:</strong> maatwebsite/excel package</li>
            <li><strong>Activity Logging:</strong> Spatie Activity Log</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Core Components</h4>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Component</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Key File</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Attendance Engine</td>
                <td>Core attendance generation and status resolution</td>
                <td><code>AttendanceService.php</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Biometric Parser</td>
                <td>Import and parse hardware device files</td>
                <td><code>BiometricImportService.php</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Leave Calculator</td>
                <td>Leave day calculations with LOP logic</td>
                <td><code>LeaveCalculationService.php</code></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Payroll API Client</td>
                <td>Integration with external Payroll system</td>
                <td><code>PayrollApiService.php</code></td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h2 id="attendance">2. Attendance Management</h2>

        <h3>Attendance Generation Process</h3>
        <p>
            The system generates attendance records for a specific month and year using the
            <code>AttendanceService::generateAttendanceRecords</code> method. This is a complex operation that considers
            multiple data sources to determine the final attendance status for each employee on each day.
        </p>

        <h4>Execution Strategy</h4>
        <div class="info-box">
            <span class="box-title">Synchronous vs Asynchronous Processing</span>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Sync Mode:</strong> When total employees ≤ 10, the system processes attendance immediately
                    within the HTTP request. This is useful for testing and small organisations.</li>
                <li><strong>Async Mode:</strong> When total employees > 10, the system chunks employees into batches of
                    100 and dispatches <code>ProcessAttendanceRecords</code> jobs to the queue. Each chunk is then
                    processed into sub-batches of 500 records.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <h4>Generation Algorithm</h4>
        <p>For every active employee, the system iterates through each day of the target month:</p>

        <ol class="step-list">
            <li><strong>Employee Validation</strong> - Skip employees without a payroll_id. Check if employee has joined
                (date_of_joining) and not resigned (date_of_resignation) for the given date.</li>
            <li><strong>Shift Resolution</strong> - Determine the employee's shift for that day by checking: (a) Duty
                Roster assignment, (b) Employee's default shift, (c) System default shift.</li>
            <li><strong>Data Collection</strong> - Fetch biometric attendance data, manual punch records, approved leave
                applications, public holidays, and week-off configuration.</li>
            <li><strong>Status Determination</strong> - Apply priority logic to determine final status (detailed below).
            </li>
            <li><strong>Record Creation</strong> - Create or update attendance_records table with calculated data.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Status Priority Logic</h3>
        <p>The system uses a waterfall model where higher priority sources override lower ones:</p>

        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Biometric Data (Highest Priority)</strong>
                <p>If a record exists in the <code>attendances</code> table (raw biometric import), it is used. The
                    status becomes <code>present</code>, <code>late</code>, or <code>early_departure</code> based on the
                    Attendance Policy rules. The system also sets flags like <code>has_biometric_data = true</code> and
                    <code>data_source = 'biometric'</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Manual Punch Data</strong>
                <p>If no biometric data exists, the system checks for approved manual punch records. If found, it uses
                    the manual punch times and sets <code>data_source = 'manual_punch'</code> with status
                    <code>present</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Leave Applications</strong>
                <p>If no punch data (biometric or manual) exists, check for approved leave applications. If the date
                    falls within a leave period, status is set to <code>absent</code> with the leave_type_id linked.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Week-off Configuration</strong>
                <p>If the date is configured as a week-off day (fetched from Payroll API), status is set to
                    <code>weekend</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Public Holidays</strong>
                <p>Check if the date is a public holiday (either fixed or flexible with approval). Status is set to
                    <code>fixed_holiday</code> or <code>flexible_holiday</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Unauthorised Absence (LOP)</strong>
                <p>If none of the above conditions match, the status defaults to <code>absent</code> with
                    <code>leave_type_id = NULL</code>. This indicates unauthorised absence and triggers Loss of Pay
                    (LOP) in salary calculation.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="warning-box">
            <span class="box-title">Hybrid Status</span>
            When an employee punches in (either biometric or manual) on a non-working day (holiday, weekend, or approved
            leave), the system creates a "hybrid" status. The actual status remains as per punch data (present/late
            etc.), but additional flags are set:
            <ul>
                <li><code>worked_on_weekend = true</code></li>
                <li><code>worked_on_holiday = true</code></li>
                <li><code>worked_on_leave = true</code></li>
                <li><code>data_source = 'hybrid'</code></li>
            </ul>
            This allows tracking of overtime work while preserving the actual attendance status.
        </div>

        <h3>Batch Management</h3>
        <p>The system uses an <code>AttendanceBatch</code> model to track generation operations:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Status Tracking:</strong> Each batch has a status (processing, completed, failed)</li>
            <li><strong>Progress Monitoring:</strong> Fields track total_records, processed_records, and failed_records
            </li>
            <li><strong>Locking:</strong> Batches can be locked to prevent further modifications</li>
            <li><strong>Audit Trail:</strong> Records who initiated the batch and when it was completed</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Attendance Locking</h3>
        <p>
            The <code>lockAttendanceRecords</code> method allows administrators to lock attendance for a specific month.
            Once locked:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Records cannot be modified or deleted</li>
            <li>The lock timestamp and user are recorded</li>
            <li>Associated batch is marked as locked and completed</li>
            <li>This ensures data integrity before payroll processing</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="biometric">3. Biometric Integration</h2>

        <h3>Supported Device Formats</h3>
        <p>The <code>BiometricImportService</code> supports multiple biometric device formats through a Strategy pattern
            implementation:</p>

        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Format Key</th>
                <th>Parser Class</th>
                <th>Vendor/Device</th>
                <th>Format Identification</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>zkteco</td>
                <td>ZKTecoParser</td>
                <td>ZKTeco devices</td>
                <td>Specific column 3 mapping for Timestamp</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>essl</td>
                <td>ESSLParser</td>
                <td>ESSL devices</td>
                <td>Proprietary header format detection</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>realtime</td>
                <td>RealtimeParser</td>
                <td>Realtime devices</td>
                <td>Realtime-specific CSV structure</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>generic_csv</td>
                <td>GenericCSVParser</td>
                <td>Any generic export</td>
                <td>Standard headers: Employee Code, Date, In Time, Out Time</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Import Process</h3>
        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>File Upload</strong>
                <p>Admin uploads a file via <code>AttendanceController::uploadBiometric</code>. The format is either
                    specified by the admin or auto-detected using parser validation.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Parser Selection</strong>
                <p>The appropriate parser is selected from the registered parsers based on format key or auto-detection.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Data Parsing</strong>
                <p>Parser reads the file and extracts records. Each parser implements the
                    <code>BiometricParserInterface</code> with <code>parse()</code> and <code>validate()</code> methods.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Record Processing</strong>
                <p>For each parsed record, the system:
                <ul>
                    <li>Validates employee existence by employee_id or payroll_id</li>
                    <li>Checks for existing manual punch (takes precedence)</li>
                    <li>Parses check-in and check-out times</li>
                    <li>Calculates total hours worked</li>
                    <li>Finds assigned shift</li>
                    <li>Applies attendance policy</li>
                    <li>Stores in <code>attendances</code> table</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="danger-box">
            <span class="box-title">Critical Constraint: Manual Punch Precedence</span>
            In the <code>BiometricImportService::processRecord</code> method, the system FIRST checks if an approved
            manual punch exists for that employee and date. If found, the biometric file data is IGNORED for that
            specific record. The manual punch is considered the corrected source of truth. This ensures HR corrections
            are never overwritten by subsequent file imports.
        </div>

        <h3>Attendance Calculation Details</h3>
        <p>The <code>calculateAttendanceDetails</code> method processes timestamps against shift and policy rules:</p>

        <h4>Late Arrival Calculation</h4>
        <pre><code>$checkInTimestamp = strtotime($checkIn);
$expectedStart = strtotime($shift->start_time);

if ($checkInTimestamp > $expectedStart) {
    $lateMinutes = ($checkInTimestamp - $expectedStart) / 60;
    // Apply grace period from policy
}</code></pre>

        <h4>Early Departure Calculation</h4>
        <pre><code>$checkOutTimestamp = strtotime($checkOut);
$expectedEnd = strtotime($shift->end_time);

if ($checkOutTimestamp < $expectedEnd) {
    $earlyMinutes = ($expectedEnd - $checkOutTimestamp) / 60;
    $undertimeHours = $earlyMinutes / 60;
}</code></pre>

        <h4>Overtime Calculation</h4>
        <pre><code>if ($checkOutTimestamp > $expectedEnd) {
    $overtimeMinutes = ($checkOutTimestamp - $expectedEnd) / 60;
    
    if ($policy->enable_overtime) {
        // Only count if beyond threshold
        if ($overtimeMinutes > $policy->overtime_start_after_minutes) {
            $actualOT = $overtimeMinutes - $policy->overtime_start_after_minutes;
            $overtimeHours = min($actualOT / 60, $policy->maximum_overtime_hours_per_day);
        }
    }
}</code></pre>

        <h3>Overtime Auto-Accumulation</h3>
        <p>
            When overtime hours are detected, the system automatically updates the monthly <code>overtime</code> record
            for the employee. It calculates the total OT hours from all attendance records for that month and updates
            the <code>calculated_ot_hours</code> field. If the policy allows auto-approval for weekend OT, the status is
            automatically set to 'approved'.
        </p>

        <h2 id="manual-punch">4. Manual Punch Control</h2>

        <h3>Purpose and Use Cases</h3>
        <p>The Manual Punch module allows HR/Admin to correct or add missing punch records when:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Biometric device malfunctions</li>
            <li>Employee forgets to punch</li>
            <li>Field employees without access to devices</li>
            <li>Network issues preventing device sync</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Workflow</h3>
        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Access Control</strong>
                <p>Only users with Admin or Super Admin roles can access manual punch features. The module is protected
                    by the <code>auth</code> and <code>admin</code> middleware.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Punch Creation</strong>
                <p>HR selects employees (single or bulk), date, shift, and punch times (in and/or out). The shift
                    dropdown is dynamically populated based on the selected date using AJAX call to
                    <code>getEmployeeShift</code>.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Validation</strong>
                <p>The system performs several critical validations before allowing manual punch creation (detailed
                    below).</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Approval Status</strong>
                <p>Manual punches are created with <code>status = 'approved'</code> by default. System also tracks
                    <code>added_by</code> user ID for audit purposes.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Critical Validation Rules</h3>

        <div class="danger-box">
            <span class="box-title">Biometric Import Timing Constraint</span>
            <strong>Rule:</strong> Manual punches CANNOT be created if biometric attendance data has already been
            imported for the target month/year.
            <br><br>
            <strong>Reason:</strong> This enforces a "Clean Data First" policy. Manual corrections must be made BEFORE
            bulk biometric import to ensure the generation process uses correct data from the start.
            <br><br>
            <strong>Implementation:</strong> The system checks two conditions:
            <pre><code>$biometricProcessed = AttendanceRecord::where('month', $month)
    ->where('year', $year)
    ->where('has_biometric_data', true)
    ->exists();

$biometricImported = Attendance::whereYear('date', $year)
    ->whereMonth('date', $month)
    ->exists();</code></pre>

            If either condition is true, the error message "Cannot create manual punch for this month. Biometric
            attendance data has already been imported..." is shown.
        </div>

        <h3>Shift Auto-Detection</h3>
        <p>The <code>getEmployeeShift</code> AJAX endpoint helps HR by auto-suggesting the shift:</p>
        <pre><code>// Checks in order:
1. Duty roster assignment for specific date
2. Employee's most recent roster (last 30 days)
3. Employee's default shift
4. System default shift</code></pre>

        <h3>Manual Punch Priority in Processing</h3>
        <p>
            When biometric files are imported AFTER manual punches exist, the <code>BiometricImportService</code> checks
            for manual punches first and uses those times instead of file data. This ensures HR corrections are never
            overwritten.
        </p>

        <h2 id="shifts">5. Shifts & Duty Rosters</h2>

        <h3>Shift Master Configuration</h3>
        <p>The <code>shifts</code> table stores shift definitions:</p>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Example</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>name</td>
                <td>Shift identifier</td>
                <td>"General Shift", "Night Shift"</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>start_time</td>
                <td>Expected start time</td>
                <td>09:00:00</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>end_time</td>
                <td>Expected end time</td>
                <td>18:00:00</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>description</td>
                <td>Additional notes</td>
                <td>Optional</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Duty Roster Management</h3>
        <p>Duty rosters allow flexible shift assignment on a per-employee, per-day basis:</p>

        <h4>Single Assignment</h4>
        <p>Admin can assign a shift to a specific employee for a specific date through
            <code>DutyRosterController::store</code>.</p>

        <h4>Bulk Assignment</h4>
        <p>The <code>bulkStore</code> method allows assigning the same shift to multiple employees across a date range:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>Select multiple employees</li>
            <li>Select a shift</li>
            <li>Define start and end dates</li>
            <li>System creates individual roster entries for each employee-date combination</li>
            <li>Existing assignments are skipped (non-destructive)</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Copy Week Functionality</h4>
        <p>The <code>copyWeek</code> feature duplicates the previous week's roster to the target week:</p>

        <pre><code>// Algorithm:
1. Calculate target week start (Monday)
2. Calculate previous week start (7 days before)
3. Fetch all rosters from previous week
4. For each roster:
   - Calculate corresponding day in target week
   - Check if assignment already exists
   - Create new assignment if not exists
5. Return summary of copied vs skipped assignments</code></pre>

        <div class="info-box">
            <span class="box-title">Week Calculation</span>
            The system uses Carbon's <code>startOfWeek()</code> which defaults to Monday as the first day of the week.
            Day of week is calculated where 0 = Sunday, 1 = Monday, etc.
        </div>

        <h4>Clear Week Functionality</h4>
        <p>The <code>clearWeek</code> method allows bulk deletion of roster assignments for a specific week. This is
            useful for resetting schedules.</p>

        <h3>Shift Resolution Logic</h3>
        <p>When processing attendance, the system determines shift using this fallback chain:</p>
        <ol>
            <li>Check <code>duty_rosters</code> table for specific employee + date</li>
            <li>If not found, check <code>duty_rosters</code> for the same employee in the last 30 days (pattern
                matching)</li>
            <li>If not found, use employee's default shift from <code>employees.shift_id</code></li>
            <li>If not found, use the first available shift in <code>shifts</code> table</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="policy">6. Attendance Policies</h2>

        <h3>Policy Configuration</h3>
        <p>The <code>AttendancePolicy</code> model contains configurable rules that govern how attendance is calculated
            and classified:</p>

        <h4>Grace Periods</h4>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Impact</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>late_arrival_grace_minutes</td>
                <td>Allowable late minutes</td>
                <td>If late by ≤ grace, treated as on-time</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>early_departure_grace_minutes</td>
                <td>Allowable early exit minutes</td>
                <td>If early by ≤ grace, no penalty</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h4>Status Thresholds</h4>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Example Value</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>half_day_late_threshold_minutes</td>
                <td>Late minutes that trigger half-day</td>
                <td>120 (2 hours)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>half_day_early_departure_threshold_minutes</td>
                <td>Early departure minutes that trigger half-day</td>
                <td>120</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>absent_threshold_minutes</td>
                <td>Late minutes that trigger absent</td>
                <td>240 (4 hours)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>minimum_work_hours_for_present</td>
                <td>Minimum total hours for present</td>
                <td>8.0</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>half_day_minimum_hours</td>
                <td>Minimum hours for half-day</td>
                <td>4.0</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h4>Overtime Configuration</h4>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Field</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>enable_overtime</td>
                <td>Master switch for OT calculation</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>overtime_start_after_minutes</td>
                <td>Minutes after shift end before OT starts</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>overtime_multiplier</td>
                <td>Pay multiplier for regular OT</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>maximum_overtime_hours_per_day</td>
                <td>Cap on daily OT hours</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>weekend_overtime_multiplier</td>
                <td>Pay multiplier for weekend OT</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>holiday_overtime_multiplier</td>
                <td>Pay multiplier for holiday OT</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>require_approval_for_overtime</td>
                <td>Whether OT needs manager approval</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h3>Status Determination Algorithm</h3>
        <p>The <code>determineStatus</code> method evaluates attendance data in this exact order:</p>

        <pre><code>function determineStatus(attendance_data):
    // 1. Check for missing punch data
    if no check_in AND no check_out:
        return 'absent'
    
    // 2. Apply grace periods
    effective_late = max(0, late_minutes - grace_period)
    effective_early_departure = max(0, early_minutes - grace_period)
    
    // 3. Check for absent (very late)
    if late_minutes >= absent_threshold:
        return 'absent'
    
    // 4. Check for insufficient work hours
    if total_hours < half_day_minimum_hours:
        return 'absent'
    
    // 5. Check for half day triggers
    if late_minutes >= half_day_late_threshold:
        return 'half_day'
    if early_departure_minutes >= half_day_early_departure_threshold:
        return 'half_day'
    if total_hours >= half_day_minimum_hours AND total_hours < minimum_work_hours:
        return 'half_day'
    
    // 6. Check for late but present
    if effective_late > 0:
        return 'late'
    
    // 7. Check for early departure
    if effective_early_departure > 0:
        return 'early_departure'
    
    // 8. Default
    return 'present'</code></pre>

        <h3>Policy Application</h3>
        <p>The system uses <code>AttendancePolicy::getActivePolicy()</code> to fetch the currently active policy. Only
            one policy can be active at a time. If no active policy is found, the first available policy is used as a
            fallback.</p>

        <h2 id="leave">7. Leave Management</h2>

        <h3>Leave Application Workflow</h3>
        <p>The system implements a multi-tier approval workflow with complex state management:</p>

        <h4>Application States</h4>
        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Status</th>
                <th>Description</th>
                <th>Next Possible States</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>pending</td>
                <td>Initial state after submission</td>
                <td>forwarded_to_manager, approved (direct HR), rejected</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>forwarded_to_manager</td>
                <td>HR has forwarded to reporting manager</td>
                <td>approved_by_manager, rejected</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>approved_by_manager</td>
                <td>Manager approved, pending HR final approval</td>
                <td>approved, rejected</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>approved</td>
                <td>Final approval by HR</td>
                <td>cancelled (by employee/admin)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>rejected</td>
                <td>Rejected at any stage</td>
                <td>Terminal state</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>cancelled</td>
                <td>Cancelled by employee or admin</td>
                <td>Terminal state</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h4>Submission Process</h4>
        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Form Submission</strong>
                <p>Employee fills leave application form with:
                <ul>
                    <li>Leave type selection</li>
                    <li>Start and end dates</li>
                    <li>Half-day options (start_half_day, end_half_day)</li>
                    <li>Reason for leave</li>
                    <li>Emergency contact details</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Leave Calculation</strong>
                <p>System calls <code>LeaveCalculationService::calculateDetailedLeaveDaysWithLOP</code> which:
                <ul>
                    <li>Iterates through each day in the date range</li>
                    <li>Excludes week-offs (from Payroll config)</li>
                    <li>Excludes public holidays</li>
                    <li>Handles half-day configurations (0.5 days)</li>
                    <li>Calculates net leave days</li>
                    <li>Checks available balance from Payroll API</li>
                    <li>Calculates LOP if balance insufficient</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>LOP Acknowledgment</strong>
                <p>If LOP days > 0:
                <pre><code>if (has_lop AND !lop_acknowledged):
    show_warning_modal()
    require_user_checkbox_confirmation()
    save lop_acknowledged = true</code></pre>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Overlap Validation</strong>
                <p>System checks for overlapping leave applications:
                <pre><code>existing_leaves = LeaveApplication
    ::where('user_id', current_user)
    ::where('status', '!=', ['rejected', 'cancelled'])
    ::where(date_range_overlaps_with_new_request)
    ::exists()</code></pre>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Record Creation</strong>
                <p>If validations pass:
                <ul>
                    <li>Create main <code>LeaveApplication</code> record</li>
                    <li>Create detailed <code>LeaveApplicationDay</code> records for each day</li>
                    <li>Log activity</li>
                    <li>Send notifications to Manager and HR</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h4>Approval Workflow</h4>
        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>Initial Review (HR/Admin)</strong>
                <p>HR can either:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Approve Directly:</strong> If no manager approval needed, HR approves immediately.
                        Status → approved.</li>
                    <li><strong>Forward to Manager:</strong> HR forwards to employee's reporting manager. Status →
                        forwarded_to_manager.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reject:</strong> HR rejects with reason. Status → rejected.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Manager Review</strong>
                <p>If forwarded, reporting manager can:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Approve:</strong> Manager approves. Status → approved_by_manager. Notification sent to
                        HR.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reject:</strong> Manager rejects with reason. Status → rejected.</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Final HR Approval</strong>
                <p>For manager-approved leaves, HR performs final review:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Approve:</strong> Final approval. Status → approved. Balance deduction initiated via
                        Payroll API.</li>
                    <li><strong>Reject:</strong> HR can still reject even after manager approval. Status → rejected.
                    </li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Leave Calculation Engine</h3>

        <h4>Day-by-Day Iteration</h4>
        <pre><code>function calculateDetailedLeaveDays(start_date, end_date, half_day_dates, user):
    current_date = start_date
    leave_days = []
    total_days = 0
    
    // Get configurations
    week_off_days = getWeekOffConfiguration(user) // [0, 6] for Sat/Sun
    public_holidays = getPublicHolidays(current_financial_year, user)
    
    while current_date <= end_date:
        day_of_week = current_date.dayOfWeek
        
        // Skip week-offs
        if day_of_week in week_off_days:
            current_date = current_date + 1 day
            continue
        
        // Initialize day data
        day_type = 'full_day'
        days_count = 1.0
        is_holiday = false
        notes = null
        
        // Check for public holiday
        if current_date in public_holidays:
            is_holiday = true
            days_count = 0
            notes = 'Public Holiday - Not counted in leave'
        
        // Check for half day
        if current_date in half_day_dates:
            day_type = half_day_dates[current_date] // 'first_half' or 'second_half'
            days_count = 0.5
        
        // Add to collection
        leave_days.append({
            'leave_date': current_date,
            'day_type': day_type,
            'days_count': days_count,
            'is_public_holiday': is_holiday,
            'notes': notes
        })
        
        total_days += days_count
        current_date = current_date + 1 day
    
    return {
        'leave_days': leave_days,
        'total_days': total_days
    }</code></pre>

        <h4>LOP Calculation</h4>
        <pre><code>function calculateLOPDetails(leave_type_id, total_days, user):
    // Fetch current balance from Payroll API
    balance_info = PayrollLeaveService.getLeaveTypeBalance(leave_type_id, user)
    available_balance = balance_info['balance']
    
    lop_days = 0
    paid_days = total_days
    has_lop = false
    
    // Check if request exceeds balance
    if total_days > available_balance:
        has_lop = true
        paid_days = max(0, available_balance)
        lop_days = total_days - paid_days
    
    return {
        'total_days': total_days,
        'paid_days': paid_days,
        'lop_days': lop_days,
        'has_lop': has_lop,
        'available_balance': available_balance
    }</code></pre>

        <h3>Leave Type Configuration</h3>
        <p>Leave types are fetched from the Payroll system via
            <code>PayrollLeaveService::getEmployeeLeaveBalance</code>. This ensures leave types and balances are always
            synchronised with the Payroll source of truth.</p>

        <h3>Notifications</h3>
        <p>The <code>LeaveNotificationService</code> handles all leave-related notifications:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>On Submission:</strong> Notify reporting manager and HR</li>
            <li><strong>On Manager Approval:</strong> Notify HR</li>
            <li><strong>On HR Approval:</strong> Notify employee</li>
            <li><strong>On Rejection:</strong> Notify employee with reason</li>
            <li><strong>On Cancellation:</strong> Notify manager and HR</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="holidays">8. Public Holiday Management</h2>

        <h3>Holiday Types</h3>
        <p>The system supports two types of public holidays:</p>

        <h4>Fixed Holidays</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Automatically available to all applicable employees</li>
            <li>No application needed</li>
            <li>Examples: Independence Day, Republic Day</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Flexible Holidays</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Require employee application and approval</li>
            <li>Managed through <code>PublicHolidayApplication</code> model</li>
            <li>Limited quota per financial year</li>
            <li>Examples: Optional regional festivals</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Department-Based Assignment</h3>
        <p>Holidays can be assigned to specific departments through the <code>department_public_holidays</code> pivot
            table. This allows different departments to have different holiday calendars.</p>

        <pre><code>// Check if holiday applicable to employee
$employee = Employee::find($employee_id);
$holiday = PublicHoliday::find($holiday_id);

$is_applicable = $holiday->departments->contains('id', $employee->department_id);</code></pre>

        <h3>Financial Year Grouping</h3>
        <p>Holidays are organised by financial year (e.g., "2024-2025"). The system automatically determines the current
            financial year based on the month:</p>
        <pre><code>function getCurrentFinancialYear():
    month = current_month()
    year = current_year()
    
    if month >= 4:  // April to March
        return "{year}-{year+1}"
    else:
        return "{year-1}-{year}"</code></pre>

        <h3>Flexible Holiday Application Workflow</h3>
        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>Employee views list of available flexible holidays for current financial year</li>
            <li>Employee applies for specific flexible holiday(s)</li>
            <li>Application is sent to Admin/HR for approval</li>
            <li>On approval, the holiday becomes active for that employee on that date</li>
            <li>Attendance generation considers approved flexible holidays same as fixed holidays</li>
        </ol>

        <h2 id="payroll-integration">9. Payroll Integration</h2>

        <h3>Integration Architecture</h3>
        <p>The Attendance system acts as a satellite module to the core Payroll system. Integration is bidirectional:
        </p>

        <div class="info-box">
            <span class="box-title">Inbound Data (Payroll → Attendance)</span>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Employees:</strong> Profile data, joining/resignation dates, department assignments</li>
                <li><strong>Departments:</strong> Organisation structure</li>
                <li><strong>Users:</strong> Login credentials synchronisation</li>
                <li><strong>Week-off Configuration:</strong> Per-employee week-off days</li>
                <li><strong>Leave Types & Balances:</strong> Available leave categories and current balances</li>
                <li><strong>Financial Year Settings:</strong> Active financial year for leave grouping</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="info-box">
            <span class="box-title">Outbound Data (Attendance → Payroll)</span>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Final Attendance Data:</strong> Locked monthly attendance status for salary calculation</li>
                <li><strong>Overtime Hours:</strong> Approved overtime for payroll processing</li>
                <li><strong>Leave Deductions:</strong> Approved leave applications for balance updates</li>
                <li><strong>LOP Days:</strong> Loss of Pay information for salary deductions</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <h3>Authentication Handshake</h3>
        <p>The system implements a "Double-Lock" security mechanism:</p>

        <ol class="step-list">
            <li>
                <strong>User Context Capture</strong>
                <p>When a user is logged into Attendance, the system captures their email address from the authenticated
                    session.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Token Request to Payroll</strong>
                <p>System sends POST request to Payroll <code>/api/login</code> endpoint:</p>
                <pre><code>Headers:
    Authorization: Bearer {JWT_SECRET_TOKEN}
    Accept: application/json

Body:
    email: {current_user_email}
    password: {current_user_password}</code></pre>
                <p>This implements two-factor verification:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Server Identity:</strong> JWT token proves the request is from trusted Attendance server
                    </li>
                    <li><strong>User Identity:</strong> Email/password validates the specific user</li>
                </ul>
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Sanctum Token Issuance</strong>
                <p>Payroll validates both factors and returns a Sanctum session token specific to that user.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Token Caching</strong>
                <p>The token is cached in Laravel cache for 23 hours:</p>
                <pre><code>$cache_key = 'payroll_api_token_' . $user->email;
Cache::put($cache_key, $sanctum_token, now()->addHours(23));</code></pre>
                <p>This reduces authentication overhead while maintaining security (tokens expire in 24 hours).</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Subsequent API Calls</strong>
                <p>All further API calls use the cached token:</p>
                <pre><code>Headers:
    Authorization: Bearer {cached_sanctum_token}
    Accept: application/json</code></pre>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h3>Employee Data Sync</h3>

        <h4>Pull Mechanism (Attendance fetches from Payroll)</h4>
        <p>The <code>PayrollApiService::getEmployees()</code> method fetches complete employee data:</p>
        <pre><code>function syncEmployeesFromPayroll():
    employees = PayrollApiService.getEmployees()
    
    for each employee in employees:
        Employee.updateOrCreate(
            ['payroll_id' => employee.payroll_id],
            [
                'employee_id' => employee.employee_id,
                'name' => employee.name,
                'email' => employee.email,
                'department_id' => employee.department_id,
                'designation' => employee.designation,
                'date_of_joining' => employee.joining_date,
                'date_of_resignation' => employee.resignation_date,
                'status' => employee.status,
                'shift_id' => employee.default_shift_id,
                'reporting_manager_payroll_id' => employee.reporting_manager
            ]
        )</code></pre>

        <h4>Push Mechanism (Payroll updates Attendance)</h4>
        <p>Payroll can push real-time updates via webhook to <code>/api/employees/sync</code>:</p>
        <pre><code>POST /api/employees/sync
Headers:
    X-API-Token: {shared_secret}
    
Body:
    {
        "employees": [
            {
                "payroll_id": "EMP001",
                "name": "John Doe",
                "email": "john@example.com",
                ...
            }
        ]
    }</code></pre>

        <h3>Leave Balance Integration</h3>
        <p>The <code>PayrollLeaveService</code> acts as a client to fetch leave data:</p>

        <h4>Get Employee Leave Balances</h4>
        <pre><code>function getEmployeeLeaveBalance(user):
    token = PayrollApiService.getToken()
    
    response = HTTP.GET(
        url: "{payroll_base_url}/api/employees/{user.email}/leave-balance",
        headers: {
            'Authorization': "Bearer {token}"
        }
    )
    
    return {
        'leave_types': response.leave_types,
        'balances': response.balances,
        'financial_year': response.financial_year
    }</code></pre>

        <h4>Week-off Configuration Fetch</h4>
        <pre><code>function getEmployeeWeekOffConfiguration(user):
    employee_data = PayrollApiService.getEmployees()
    
    employee = find_by_email(employee_data, user.email)
    
    if employee.week_off_configuration exists:
        return {
            'week_off_days': employee.week_off_configuration.days,  // e.g., [0, 6]
            'source': 'payroll_api'
        }
    else:
        return {
            'week_off_days': [0, 6],  // Default Sat/Sun
            'source': 'default_fallback'
        }</code></pre>

        <h2 id="sync">10. Data Synchronisation</h2>

        <h3>Sync Controllers</h3>
        <p>The system provides multiple sync controllers for different entities:</p>

        <h4>Employee Sync</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Controller:</strong> <code>EmployeeSyncController</code></li>
            <li><strong>Route:</strong> <code>/admin/employees/sync</code></li>
            <li><strong>Function:</strong> Pulls all employees from Payroll and updates local database</li>
            <li><strong>Frequency:</strong> Manual trigger or scheduled via cron</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Department Sync</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Controller:</strong> <code>DepartmentSyncController</code></li>
            <li><strong>Route:</strong> <code>/admin/departments/sync</code></li>
            <li><strong>Function:</strong> Synchronises department structure</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>User Sync</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Controller:</strong> <code>UserSyncController</code></li>
            <li><strong>Route:</strong> <code>/admin/users/sync</code></li>
            <li><strong>Function:</strong> Synchronises user login credentials and passwords</li>
            <li><strong>Special:</strong> Includes password sync to maintain single login across systems</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>API Sync Controller</h3>
        <p>The <code>ApiSyncController</code> handles incoming webhooks from Payroll:</p>

        <table>
            <tr>
                <th>Endpoint</th>
                <th>Method</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>Security</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>/api/employees/sync</td>
                <td>POST</td>
                <td>Receive employee updates from Payroll</td>
                <td>X-API-Token header</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>/api/departments/sync</td>
                <td>POST</td>
                <td>Receive department updates</td>
                <td>X-API-Token header</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>/api/users/sync-password</td>
                <td>POST</td>
                <td>Sync password changes</td>
                <td>JWT Token</td>
            </tr>
        </table>

        <h2 id="reports">11. Reports & Analytics</h2>

        <h3>Attendance Summary Report</h3>
        <p>The <code>getAttendanceSummary</code> method in <code>AttendanceService</code> generates comprehensive
            monthly reports:</p>

        <h4>Data Points Per Employee</h4>
        <ul>
            <li>Total days in month</li>
            <li>Present days (including late, early departure)</li>
            <li>Leave days (breakdown by leave type)</li>
            <li>Weekend days</li>
            <li>Public holiday days</li>
            <li>Absent days (unauthorised)</li>
            <li>LOP days (total from leaves + unauthorised absences)</li>
            <li>Salary days (Total days - LOP days)</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>LOP Calculation in Reports</h4>
        <pre><code>function calculateEmployeeLOPForMonth(employee, month, year):
    // LOP from leave applications
    leave_lop = LeaveApplication
        ::where('email_id', employee.email)
        ::forMonth(month, year)
        ::where('has_lop', true)
        ::sum('lop_days')
    
    // LOP from unauthorised absences
    absence_lop = AttendanceRecord
        ::where('payroll_id', employee.payroll_id)
        ::forMonth(month, year)
        ::where('status', 'absent')
        ::where('leave_type_id', NULL)
        ::count()
    
    total_lop = leave_lop + absence_lop
    salary_days = days_in_month - total_lop
    
    return {
        'lop_days': total_lop,
        'salary_days': salary_days
    }</code></pre>

        <h3>Reports Controller</h3>
        <p>The <code>ReportsController</code> provides various report views:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Monthly attendance summary</li>
            <li>Leave balance report</li>
            <li>Overtime summary</li>
            <li>Late arrival trends</li>
            <li>Department-wise attendance statistics</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="admin">12. Administrative Tools</h2>

        <h3>Bulk Attendance Regeneration</h3>
        <p>The <code>regenerate</code> method allows admins to recalculate attendance for a month:</p>

        <pre><code>function regenerate(month, year):
    // Step 1: Delete existing unlocked records
    AttendanceRecord.forMonthYear(month, year)
        .unlocked()
        .delete()
    
    // Step 2: Generate fresh records
    AttendanceService.generateAttendanceRecords(month, year, current_admin_id)
    
    return redirect_to_preview()</code></pre>

        <div class="warning-box">
            <span class="box-title">Regeneration Rules</span>
            <ul>
                <li>Only <strong>unlocked</strong> records are deleted. Locked records are preserved for data integrity.
                </li>
                <li>Useful when: Shift policies change, Manual punches are corrected, Duty rosters are updated</li>
                <li>The operation is non-destructive for locked months (typically previous months already processed for
                    payroll)</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <h3>Diagnostic Tools</h3>

        <h4>Diagnose Month Leaves</h4>
        <p>The <code>diagnoseMonthLeaves</code> endpoint helps debug leave-attendance discrepancies:</p>
        <pre><code>GET /admin/attendance/diagnose-month-leaves?month=8&year=2025

Returns JSON with:
{
    "leaves_count": 15,
    "leaves": [
        {
            "id": 123,
            "user": {...},
            "period": {
                "start_date": "2025-08-01",
                "end_date": "2025-08-05",
                "days_count": 5
            },
            "leave_type": {...},
            "attendance_records": {
                "count": 5,
                "records": [
                    {
                        "date": "2025-08-01",
                        "status": "absent",
                        "leave_type_id": 2
                    },
                    ...
                ]
            },
            "expected_dates": ["2025-08-01", "2025-08-02", ...]
        }
    ]
}</code></pre>

        <p>This helps identify cases where:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Approved leave exists but attendance record shows LOP</li>
            <li>Leave type mismatch between application and record</li>
            <li>Missing attendance records for leave dates</li>
        </ul>

        <h4>Diagnose Single Leave</h4>
        <p>For deeper investigation of a specific leave application, use <code>diagnoseLeave</code> endpoint.</p>

        <h3>Attendance Override</h3>
        <p>The <code>AttendanceOverrideController</code> allows manual corrections to specific attendance records after
            generation. This is useful for exceptional cases that automated logic cannot handle.</p>

        <h3>Activity Logs</h3>
        <p>The system uses Spatie Activity Log package to track all critical actions:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Attendance record modifications</li>
            <li>Leave application status changes</li>
            <li>Manual punch creations/deletions</li>
            <li>Policy changes</li>
            <li>Roster assignments</li>
        </ul>

        <p>Logs include:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Who performed the action (causer_id)</li>
            <li>What was changed (properties, old & new values)</li>
            <li>When it occurred (created_at)</li>
            <li>Description of the event</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="api">13. API Reference</h2>

        <h3>Authentication API</h3>
